1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:11,614
This is a recording of the real Angular billing component, driven over the DevTools protocol, against a small mock server that plays our API and Razorpay.

2
00:00:11,614 --> 00:00:13,837
Nothing here touches Razorpay.

3
00:00:14,937 --> 00:00:22,101
The page loads the plans, the subscription, the AutoPay availability and the current mandate.

4
00:00:22,101 --> 00:00:28,649
Availability is true, so a paid plan's button reads Subscribe now instead of Upgrade.

5
00:00:30,162 --> 00:00:32,575
Subscribe opens a confirmation.

6
00:00:32,575 --> 00:00:39,504
On confirm, the component posts only the plan id to billing slash autopay slash checkout.

7
00:00:39,504 --> 00:00:47,834
The server computes the amount from the database, with tax, and creates the Razorpay plan and subscription.

8
00:00:50,708 --> 00:00:56,419
The response carries the authorisation URL, which opens in a new tab.

9
00:00:56,419 --> 00:00:59,895
The component then reads the mandate back.

10
00:00:59,895 --> 00:01:07,675
Its status is Pending authorization, and the plan access is untouched: no payment, no credits.

11
00:01:09,183 --> 00:01:11,753
The mock now moves the mandate on.

12
00:01:11,753 --> 00:01:18,934
The component is polling the refresh endpoint every five seconds, and the server asks Razorpay.

13
00:01:18,934 --> 00:01:21,807
It shows Payment pending, then Active.

14
00:01:21,807 --> 00:01:29,215
Only on that transition does it reload the subscription, the payment history and the entitlements.

15
00:01:30,714 --> 00:01:39,607
The history row comes from the payments endpoint, with the new optional fields: method, transaction id and status.

16
00:01:41,107 --> 00:01:46,812
Invoices are read from Razorpay through the server on demand, not stored.

17
00:01:46,812 --> 00:01:50,015
Each row links to Razorpay's hosted page.

18
00:01:51,525 --> 00:01:59,341
A failed payment is recorded server side as a Failed payment row, matched to the mandate through its invoice.

19
00:01:59,341 --> 00:02:06,153
The mandate is Pending at Razorpay, which the screen shows as Past due, with the retry message.

20
00:02:06,153 --> 00:02:10,312
The failed row is listed with its reason and is not money.

21
00:02:11,813 --> 00:02:15,962
After a successful retry the mandate is Active again.

22
00:02:15,962 --> 00:02:19,015
Cancel posts cancel at cycle end, true.

23
00:02:19,015 --> 00:02:26,294
The server records that the plan will not renew, and the screen shows Cancellation scheduled.

24
00:02:26,294 --> 00:02:33,104
Whether Razorpay honours cancel at cycle end for UPI mandates is still to be confirmed.

25
00:02:34,618 --> 00:02:42,244
What this does not show: Razorpay's real responses, a UPI app, webhooks arriving, or the database.

26
00:02:42,244 --> 00:02:52,983
Those are covered by the backend tests with a fake gateway, and by the manual checklist in the testing document, which is still to be run.

